opular was she? Immensely.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<br />Sometimes an adverb of manner is placed before a verb + object to add emphasis. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example:<br /><span class=\"italic\"> She boldly decided to become a famous actress.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<br />Many adverbs are formed by adding <span class=\"italic\">-ly</span> to an adjective."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Examples:<br /><span class=\"italic\"> bold \u2192 boldly     &nbsp; &nbsp;                  happy \u2192 happily</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": " <br />Some adverbs are formed by adding <span class=\"italic\">-ally</span>. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example:<br /> <span class=\"italic\">general \u2192 generally       &nbsp; &nbsp;      beautiful \u2192 beautifully</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Examples:<br />  <span class=\"italic\">She was famously referred to as \u201cLittle Eva.\u201d<br /> She spoke quickly.</span>"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to serve"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to spend a period of time doing work for a country"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: She spent her time serving the citizens of Argentina."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le02ob03aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about personal qualities."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "First Lady"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the wife of the leader of a country"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: She became Argentina's First Lady in 1946."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le02ob03aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "bold"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "not afraid of taking risks and making difficult decis