"id": 0, "_data": []}, {"contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"coverimg": "engenn6le02ob03re2img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "engenn6le02ob03re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "engenn6le02ob03re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"time": "100", "image": "engenn6le02ob03re2img01.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "Eva Peron, or more famously referred to as Evita, which means \u201cLittle Eva\u201d served as Argentina's First Lady between 1946 and 1952. She loved drama and acting at school. The cinema fascinated her and she boldly decided to become a famous actress."}, {"time": "21000", "image": "engenn6le02ob03re2img02.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "Eva left her small village when she was 15, in search of the bright lights in the big city. She made her acting debut in 1935 and naturally joined a theatre company. In 1942, she had a breakthrough when she signed a five-year contract with Radio Belgrano. Within a year, she was one of the highest paid radio actresses in Argentina."}, {"time": "44000", "image": "engenn6le02ob03re2img03.jpg", "id": 3, "text": "In 1944, Eva met Juan Peron and they were married a year later. In 1946, Eva became Argentina's First Lady. She was charismatic, fiery and immensely popular with the poor, who nicknamed her Evita. She died at the age of 33. Her rags-to-riches life was turned into musicals and movies, which eventually made her famous worldwide."}]}}], "template_override": 1, "title": "", "type": "audio", "id": 1, "_data": []}], "id": 0, "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}], "type": "lab_options"}]}]}